    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8583" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεψι-ός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>first cousin,</i> or generally,
				<i>cousin,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.464
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.30
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				7.82
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				856
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				58D.
			</span></i>, etc., v. esp. <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.47
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πρὸς πατρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Is.
					11.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ πατρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					22.170
				</span></i>
			: comically, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγχέλεων ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Stratt.
					39
				</span></i>
			. [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεψιοῦ κταμένοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.554
				</span></i>
			, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεψιόο κτ.</span>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				3.295
			</span></i>.] (Cf. Skt. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναπᾱτ</span> 'grandson',
			Lat. <i>nepos,</i> etc.)</div>
